  "description": "Roubaix is an aluminum- framed\n\nbicycle, but it's not made from just any aluminum, no way. It's made from\n\nFuji's Lite Custom butted and tapered aluminum tubes in five diameters. The\n\nresult: A light, quick, responsive frame that feels alive under you.\n\nLike Roubaix Pros, Roubaixs have a Fuji carbon fiber fork with alloy steerer,\n\ncool Ritchey Pro Road wheels, Shimano brakes and shifting parts, Kore bar\n\nand Fuji Superlight stem, Michelin Axial Performance tires and Time MID clipless\n\npedals.\n\nRoubaix bicycles have triple cranksets, three gear choices in the front and\n\nnine in the rear. The third chainring is smaller than the small one on a\n\ntwo-ring bike. It provides lots of low gears for steep climbs and the last\n\n15 tired miles of a 100-miler.\n\nA Roubaix will feel totally responsive, as if every bit of effort you put\n\ninto the pedals moves you irresistibly forward. It'll feel light and quick\n\nand solid.\n\nAnd it'll have three chainrings. That third ring won't matter much crossing\n\nIowa on RAGBRAI. It's a good friend in the Rockies, though.",
